{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall engrave upon them.</b> And further on it is written: ״והאבנים תהיינה על שמות בני ישראל״ etc. If so, the verses contradict each other. Rather, it teaches that the letters were not protruding but were sunk into the stones, and were thus protruding on the inside, above the names — here and there from the letters. Accordingly you find the names upon the stones and the stones upon the names."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הילך והילך מן האותיות' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The sense appears to be that the stone material protrudes here and there around the engraved letters."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:09.950792300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}